= Bringing back the left-communists?

Quite miraculously, the previously dead left-communist wing of our party has been revitalized. Some of our expelled leaders and members have expressed interest in rejoining. IF this is allowed, it will mean almost certain expulsion from the Comintern and factional infighting may become nearly unmanagable. 

- @reintegrate: We will allow them back in.
- @reject: Our party cannot be led by these Trotskyists, purge the party a second time!

@reintegrate
on-arrival: left_opposition_dissent += 10; marxist_leninist_dissent += 10; conciliators_strength += 10; right_opposition_strength -= 10; spd_relation += 10; left_split_fixed = 1; workers_kpd += 2; unemployed_kpd += 2; n_advisors -= 1 if zetkin_advisor == 1; zetkin_advisor = 0;  n_advisors -= 1 if brandler_advisor == 1; brandler_advisor = 0; n_advisors -= 1 if thalheimer_advisor == 1; thalheimer_advisor = 0; n_advisors -= 1 if frolich_advisor == 1; frolich_advisor = 0; n_advisors -= 1 if munzenberg_advisor == 1; munzenberg_advisor = 0; n_advisors -= 1 if meyer_advisor == 1; meyer_advisor = 0; n_advisors -= 1 if eberlein_advisor == 1;  eberlein_advisor = 0; n_advisors -= 1 if ewert_advisor == 1 ewert_advisor = 0

Through our influence, the united front is retained. Many are opposed to this but democratic centralism puts them in line soon enough. Much of the Conciliators and Right Oppositions have either been expelled or removed from leadership.

@reject
on-arrival: left_opposition_strength -= 80; left_opposition_dissent += 100; marxist_leninist_dissent -= 10; right_opposition_dissent -= 10; conciliator_dissent -= 10

We reject any notion of reintegrating the expelled left-communists. We purge the party again to ensure such a sentiment doesn't rise again.

